## Environment

Fill in only when the project has non-obvious requirements, so an agent can tell a check it cannot run from a check that failed:

- runtime and toolchain versions, and the lockfiles that pin dependencies;
- OS or hardware requirements;
- required environment variables, by name only, never values;
- external services, and the fixtures or test doubles that stand in for them;
- what each environment (local machines, CI, remote agents) can and cannot run.

A check an environment cannot run is recorded as `NOT RUN` with the reason, never as `FAIL`.

